{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-01T10:57:52.974Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"489489c9e2938b0738fed20a","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1647","lineage:pm-gh1647","lineage:pm-dj98","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"pm-gh1647","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1647","lineage:pm-gh1647","lineage:pm-dj98","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.316","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-fr10t8"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"A continuable key=value prose segment containing a colon is misread as a new key, so --comment/--note/--learning seeds store the raw entry with its text= prefix"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"The shared key=value grammar (parseCsvKv in src/core/item/parse.ts) splits a continuable prose value on commas and then treats any later segment containing a colon or equals sign as a NEW key, even when the candidate key is not an identifier. For --comment, --note and --learning seeds, parseLogSeed then sees an \"unsupported key\" and falls back to storing the whole raw entry, so the immutable comment keeps the literal text= prefix the agent wrote as syntax.\n\nReproduced on pm 2026.11.1 in a sandbox: pm create --title t --type Task --comment \"text=(a, b) c. Related: d\" stores \"text=(a, b) c. Related: d\". The segment \" b) c. Related: d\" is parsed as key \"b) c. Related\" with value \"d\". \"text=a. Related: b\" (no comma) and \"text=a (b, c); d\" (no colon after the comma) both round-trip correctly, which is why the defect only shows up in longer prose. Observed in practice on pm-gh1647: its create-time intake comment is stored with a text= prefix.\n\npm-hu92i3 fixed the three comma behaviours (whitespace, escapes, quotes) but not this delimiter-in-continuation case. The markdown-line parser already requires keys to match [A-Za-z0-9_.-]+; the CSV path does not."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","annotations","cli","data-integrity","parsing"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-01T10:57:52.974Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-01T10:57:52.974Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":45},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"parseCsvKv treats a segment whose candidate key is not an identifier ([A-Za-z0-9_.-]+) as a continuation of the active continuable key instead of a new key; pm create --comment/--note/--learning with text=(a, b) c. Related: d stores exactly (a, b) c. Related: d; no stored log seed ever keeps a literal text= prefix when the text key parsed; GH-258 strict unknown-key rejection still refuses an identifier-shaped typo key such as lable=main"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-yql1"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Prose values containing commas followed by colons round-trip byte-identically through every key=value annotation seed."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"pm create --comment \"text=(a, b) c. Related: d\" stores the comment text as \"text=(a, b) c. Related: d\"."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-gh1647","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-01T10:57:52.974Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-hu92i3","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-01T10:57:52.974Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/escape_class","value":"production_defect"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"e1ca1d64b922d1f73adf91d784c83e225c222fd1fb6c96d09e0991e8f5330cf9","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"f79cbb2729ebe3af97402a5c9ecfae20fb10c573beed376f96619a4da1464169"}
